[?2004l[?2004h>       "status": "ANSWERED",
[?2004l[?2004h>       "answer": "PAXLOVID contains ritonavir, which is a strong CYP3A inhibitor. This can lead to increased plasma concentrations of concomitant medications metabolized by CYP3A, potentially resulting in severe, life-threatening, or fatal events. Conversely, concomitant use of strong CYP3A inducers can decrease PAXLOVID concentrations, leading to a loss of therapeutic effect and the potential development of viral resistance. Commonly reported serious adverse reactions due to interactions include calcineurin inhibitors (e.g., tacrolimus, cyclosporine) and calcium channel blockers. Prior to prescribing, healthcare providers must review all medications to assess potential interactions and determine if dose adjustments, interruptions, or additional monitoring are required.",
