[?2004lin[?2004h>       "answer": "Medications that should be avoided (contraindicated) with PAXLOVID include drugs primarily metabolized by CYP3A for which elevated concentrations are associated with serious and/or life-threatening reactions, and strong CYP3A inducers which significantly reduce PAXLOVID plasma concentrations. Examples of medications to avoid include: alfuzosin, ranolazine, amiodarone, dronedarone, flecainide, propafenone, quinidine, colchicine (in renal/hepatic impairment), lurasidone, pimozide, silodosin, eplerenone, ivabradine, dihydroergotamine, ergotamine, methylergonovine, lovastatin, simvastatin, voclosporin, lomitapide, eletriptan, ubrogepant, finerenone, naloxegol, sildenafil (for PAH), triazolam, oral midazolam, flibanserin, and tolvaptan. Strong CYP3A inducers to avoid include apalutamide, enzalutamide, carbamazepine, phenobarbital, primidone, phenytoin, rifampin, rifapentine, lumacaftor/ivacaftor, and St. John's Wort.",
