[?2004latening reactions; and 3) Co[?2004h>       "answer": "The important warnings and precautions associated with PAXLOVID include: 1) Risk of serious adverse reactions due to drug interactions (strong CYP3A inhibition of concomitant drugs or reduction of PAXLOVID concentrations by inducers); 2) Hypersensitivity reactions, including anaphylaxis, toxic epidermal necrolysis (TEN), and Stevens-Johnson syndrome; 3) Hepatotoxicity, including hepatic transaminase elevations, clinical hepatitis, and jaundice; and 4) Risk of HIV-1 resistance development in individuals with uncontrolled or undiagnosed HIV-1 infection.",
