[?2004lrtin[?2004h>       "answer": "PAXLOVID should not be taken by: 1) Patients with a history of clinically significant hypersensitivity reactions (such as toxic epidermal necrolysis or Stevens-Johnson syndrome) to nirmatrelvir, ritonavir, or any other components of the product; 2) Patients taking medications that are contraindicated due to CYP3A metabolism or strong CYP3A induction; and 3) Patients with severe hepatic impairment (Child-Pugh Class C), for whom PAXLOVID is not recommended. Additionally, although not contraindicated, PAXLOVID is not recommended for pediatric patients as the optimal dose has not been established.",
