[?2004l[?2004h>       "status": "ANSWERED",
[?2004l[?2004h>       "answer": "The recommended dosage for PAXLOVID is 300 mg nirmatrelvir (two 150 mg tablets) with 100 mg ritonavir (one 100 mg tablet), with all 3 tablets taken together orally twice daily (morning and bedtime) for 5 days. For patients with moderate renal impairment (eGFR >=30 to <60 mL/min), the dosage is reduced to 150 mg nirmatrelvir (one 150 mg tablet) and 100 mg ritonavir (one 100 mg tablet) twice daily for 5 days. For patients with severe renal impairment (eGFR <30 mL/min), the dose and dose frequency are reduced (300 mg nirmatrelvir and 100 mg ritonavir on Day 1, and 150 mg nirmatrelvir and 100 mg ritonavir on Days 2-5).",
